1. **A (meth)acryloyl compound** represented by formula (A):

\[
\mathrm{Z}\left[-\mathrm{X}-\left(\mathrm{R}^{1A}\mathrm{O}\right)_k-\mathrm{C(=O)-C(R^1)=CH_2}\right]_p
\tag{A}
\]

wherein:

- **R¹** is hydrogen or a C₁-C₆ alkyl group, preferably hydrogen or methyl;

- **R¹A** is independently, at each occurrence, a substituted or unsubstituted divalent hydrocarbon group, optionally containing one or more heteroatoms selected from oxygen, sulfur, nitrogen, silicon, and phosphorus, and preferably is a C₁-C₂₀ alkylene, C₃-C₂₀ cycloalkylene, C₆-C₂₀ arylene, C₇-C₂₀ aralkylene, polyoxyalkylene, or siloxane-containing divalent group;

- **X** is independently, at each occurrence, a single bond or a divalent linking group selected from substituted or unsubstituted alkylene, alkenylene, alkynylene, cycloalkylene, arylene, heteroarylene, ether, ester, carbonate, carbamate, urea, amide, thioether, sulfone, siloxane, and combinations thereof;

- **Z** is a p-valent organic or organosilicon residue derived from an alcohol, phenol, amine, thiol, epoxy compound, isocyanate compound, carboxylic acid, silane, siloxane, polyether, polyester, polycarbonate, polyurethane, polyamide, polyolefin, polysiloxane, or dendritic, hyperbranched, or polymeric core;

- **k** is independently, at each occurrence, an integer of 0 to 100;

- **m** is an integer of 0 to 50;

- **n** is an integer of 0 to 50; and

- **p** is an integer of 1 to 20,

provided that the compound contains at least one (meth)acryloyl group.

A suitable Markush description may be written as follows:

**A multifunctional (meth)acryloyl monomer** represented by Formula (I):

\[
A\left[-X-(CH_2)_k-\left(CR^3R^4\right)_m-\left(OCH_2CH(R^5)\right)_n-O-C(O)-C(R^1)=CH_2\right]_p
\]

wherein:

- **A** is a polyvalent organic core having a valency of **p**, selected from substituted or unsubstituted:
  - linear or branched aliphatic groups having **1 to 40 carbon atoms**,
  - cycloaliphatic groups having **3 to 20 carbon atoms**,
  - aryl groups having **6 to 30 carbon atoms**,
  - aralkyl or alkaryl groups having **7 to 30 carbon atoms**,
  - heteroatom-containing groups containing one or more O, N, S, Si, or P atoms, and having **2 to 40 carbon atoms**;

- **X** is independently at each occurrence a direct bond, —O—, —S—, —NR^2—, —C(O)O—, —OC(O)—, —C(O)NR^2—, —NR^2C(O)—, urethane, carbonate, ester, ether, thioether, amide, urea, or siloxane linkage;

- **R^1** is independently hydrogen or methyl, such that the terminal group is an acryloyl or methacryloyl group;

- **R^2** is hydrogen, alkyl having **1 to 12 carbon atoms**, aryl having **6 to 18 carbon atoms**, or aralkyl having **7 to 18 carbon atoms**;

- **R^3** and **R^4** are independently hydrogen, halogen, hydroxyl, alkyl having **1 to 12 carbon atoms**, alkoxy having **1 to 12 carbon atoms**, cycloalkyl having **3 to 12 carbon atoms**, aryl having **6 to 18 carbon atoms**, or together form a cycloalkyl ring having **3 to 12 carbon atoms**;

- **R^5** is independently hydrogen, methyl, ethyl, propyl, or alkyl having **1 to 6 carbon atoms**;

- each alkyl, cycloalkyl, aryl, aralkyl, alkoxy, or heteroatom-containing group may be optionally substituted with one or more substituents selected from halogen, hydroxyl, cyano, nitro, amino, alkylamino, dialkylamino, alkoxy, aryloxy, alkylthio, arylthio, ester, carbonate, carbamate, amide, urea, sulfonyl, phosphonate, silane, siloxane, epoxy, oxetanyl, or additional ethylenically unsaturated groups;

- **k** is an integer from **0 to 20**;

- **m** is an integer from **0 to 20**;

- **n** is an integer from **0 to 100**;

- **p** is an integer from **2 to 10**, preferably **2 to 6**, representing the number of independently selected (meth)acryloyl-functional arms attached to A;

provided that the compound contains at least two terminal acryloyl or methacryloyl groups.

A (meth)acryloyl compound represented by the following formula (A):

\[
\mathrm{CH_2=C(R^1)-C(=O)-O-L-X}
\tag{A}
\]

wherein R¹ represents a hydrogen atom or a methyl group; L represents a divalent linking group selected from a substituted or unsubstituted C1-C20 alkylene group, a substituted or unsubstituted C6-C20 arylene group, a substituted or unsubstituted C7-C30 aralkylene group, and a group comprising at least one of an ether bond, an ester bond, a carbonate bond, a urethane bond, an amide bond, a thioether bond, or a siloxane bond; and X represents a functional group selected from an epoxy group, an oxetanyl group, a hydroxyl group, a carboxyl group, an amino group, an isocyanate group, a blocked isocyanate group, an alkoxysilyl group, a fluorinated alkyl group, a phosphoric acid group, a sulfonic acid group, and a polymerizable ethylenically unsaturated group, provided that the compound contains at least one (meth)acryloyl group and has a molecular weight of 150 to 5,000.
